One important distinction

The public K&D experience is now GitHub-ready and launchable immediately.

The only V3 features that cannot be made genuinely secure with GitHub Pages alone are cloud player accounts, synchronized collections, a secure web-based Owner Command Center, stored customer orders, real online order tracking, stored form submissions, browser image uploads, and genuinely private Vault-code validation. GitHub Pages is static hosting, so those require an external backend if we want them later.

I deliberately didn't make fake security and pretend static JavaScript could safely handle that stuff.

But this version gets us exactly where you asked:

UPLOAD → COMMIT → PUSH → LIVE.
